  "description": "Your SLR Sram\n\nTHE LATEST EVOLUTION OF OUR UNIQUE MASON SLR, WITH CONFIGURABLE SRAM BUILD OPTIONS\n\nThe new MASON SLR steel modern super-tourer is the result of our focus on ride quality, long-distance performance, and luxury grand-touring capabilities. A new chapter in Mason Cycles’ obsession with high-performance steel, designed in collaboration with one of the most skilled and established bicycle frame builders in Italy - Cicli Barco.\n\nSimply stunning from every aspect, thanks to exceptional ride quality and attention to detail that sets it above the rest. In my opinion, it's faultless.\n\nRoad.cc ROAD BIKE OF THE YEAR AND OVERALL WINNER - BIKE OF THE YEAR 2022/23\n\nThe capacity for 700C x 40mm tyres, including full fenders and multiple attachment points for accessories and carriers gives the SLR wide ranging, all-condition, and long-distance capability - from refined grand-touring to fast cross-country and multi-day adventures.\n\nThe SLR tube set makes for an engaging and comfortable ride with an emphasis on smooth, fast travel. The custom shaped, progressively-butted, phosphate-coated Dedacciai Zero/Zero Uno tube set is made exclusively for the SLR frame. It offers class-leading compliance and weight, combined with a propulsive, plush ride quality, and maximum pedalling efficiency.\n\nPaired with a new MASON full-carbon fork, the RangeFinder AR [‘AR’ for AllRoad] - which is tuned for all-conditions riding on firmer surfaces with large tyres. The RangeFinder AR features a set of molded-in eyelets which are designed to be fitted with a front rack or rando-style bag support, in addition to an internally-routed dynamo front light.\n\n100% Italian TIG-welded/silver-brazed frame manufacturing, wet-painting, and finishing.\n\nSelect From: SRAM Rival AXS / Force AXS / Red AXS, including 1x XPLR gearing options.\n\nThis bike can be fitted with the Mason Luminance Upgrade. The ultimate dynamo + lighting set-up for all-terrain and multi-surface adventures. See 'Accessories + Upgrades' for details.\n\nChoices of Schwalbe, Rene Herse and Continental tubeless tyres designed for maximum speed, ride quality and all-surface control.\n\nChain pip neatly holds the chain and retains it on the chainring whilst the wheel is removed for transport.\n\nDiscrete internal dynamo-light routing in top-tube with stainless-steel port reinforcement as standard.\n\nClearance for 50/34T double chainrings.\n\nDedacciai Zero Uno seat tube with flush-fitting alloy reduction sleeve for 27.2mm seat post.\n\nModern 1-1/8” - 1.5” tapered Dedacciai Zero Uno head tube with integrated Deda head set.\n\nEuropean-made, exclusively custom shaped and formed, phosphate anti-corrosion treated Dedacciai Zero/Zero Uno tube set.",
